          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Apple's iOS 27 to let users choose their own AI model for Siri tasks, opening system to third parties",
            "articleSection": "Daily Utility",
            "abstract": "Apple is reportedly planning to redesign iOS 27 so that users can select from a range of third-party AI models to power tasks across the operating system, moving away from a single default model approach. The change would allow consumers to pick models from competing providers for functions like writing assistance, summarisation, and smart replies. This would represent a fundamental shift in how Apple controls the AI layer of its devices and could reshape competition among AI model providers.",
            "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/05/apple-plans-to-make-ios-27-a-choose-your-own-adventure-of-ai-models/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
